  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [Design and Access Statement, 25993-PL-00, 25993-PL-S-01, 25993-PL-01, 25993-PL-02, 25993-PL-03, 25993-PL04, 25993-PL05. Received: 18/08/2025. 25993-PL-S-02 Rev A, 2512047-TK01 Rev A. Received: 06/01/2026].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - Either side of the vehicle access, visibility splay areas (the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access, with a splay of at least 2.4 metres x 2.4 metres) shall be provided before the access and parking area is brought into use.  These areas shall be kept clear of any obstructions to visibility greater than 600 mm in height, including shrubs, planting, boundary walls, fences, gates, other means of enclosure or other structures or objects at all times.\r\nReason:  To ensure adequate visibility for drivers entering and leaving the site in the interests of pedestrian and vehicle safety.",
    "Condition : 5 - No building or use hereby permitted shall be occupied or use commenced until the parking spaces (including spaces for people with disabilities have been marked out and provided in accordance with the scheme shown on drawing No. 25993-PL-S-02 Rev A.  This provision shall be permanently available for the occupiers and users of the premises and used for no other purpose.  \r\nReason:  To ensure that there are adequate servicing facilities within the site in the interests of highway safety\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to the hereby approved development being brought into use, details of secure, covered cycle parking facilities for staff and visitors shall be submitted to, and approved in writing by, the Local Planning Authority. The facilities shall conform to the current Westtrans West London Cycle Parking Guidance (or such other guidance as shall supersede it) in design and layout and be fully implemented and made available for use before the first occupation of the development or commencement of the approved use as appropriate and thereafter retained for use at all times without obstruction. \r\nReason: In order to support sustainable transport objectives."
  ],
